cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "triplet-proof: code and data for 'Error robustness of doublet and triplet genetic codes'"
abstract: >-
  Code, verification checks and outputs for the revised manuscript "Error
  robustness of doublet and triplet genetic codes". The minimum per-residue
  cost of single-nucleotide misreading at fixed amino-acid usage does not
  depend on codon length; a longer code gains only by silencing its noisiest
  position. Version 2.0.0 withdraws the conclusion of v1.0.0, whose z-scores
  came from a codon-shuffling null that measures synonym clustering.
type: software
